;
SAVING AND LOADING AUTH SETTINGS

A - The startup policy
B - Command files and recovery
:A
THE STARTUP POLICY

AUTH /SAVE saves the live map; AUTH /LOAD restores a saved map.
The default filename at either prompt is I13:AUTH.DAT.
BYE reads that file when it initializes. Unsaved changes survive
calls but are lost when the saved policy is reloaded or BYE restarts.

The files contain the drive and DU map, not F4 approvals.
An alternate file may be loaded without changing the startup name.
:B
COMMAND FILES AND RECOVERY

AUTH /SAVE=I13:AUTH.DAT /Y
AUTH /LOAD=I13:AUTH.DAT

An explicit filename avoids interactive filename prompts.
/Y permits overwriting an existing destination for SAVE only.
Without /Y an explicit SAVE to an existing file fails.

The previous saved policy is retained as AUTH.BAK. A failed write
may leave a temporary file. Preserve it for inspection rather than
blindly removing it. Use AUTH to manage binary policy files.

Loading a policy does not undo F4 changes. See HELP AUTH.
